      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\) and the requirement \\(x \\neq 1\\). We need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the sum in a more convenient form. The sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is a geometric series with the first term 1 and common ratio \\(x\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{x^n - 1}{x - 1}\n\\]\n\nIn our case, the series starts from \\(x^{2016}\\) and includes all terms up to \\(x\\), so there are 2017 terms. Therefore, the sum is:\n\n\\[\nS_{2017} = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}\n\\]\n\nWe know from the given equation that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Substituting this into the sum, we get:\n\n\\[\nS_{2017} = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
