      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\n\\[x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0.\\]\n\nThis can be rearranged to:\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nTo find the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\), we use the fact that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Notice that the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is the sum of a geometric series with the first term 1 and common ratio \\(x\\), for 2017 terms. The sum of this geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[\\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nFrom the given equation, we know that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Therefore, substituting \\(x^{2017}\\) into the sum formula, we get:\n\n\\[\\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
