      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to:\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe want to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). This sum can be rewritten using the fact that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Notice that:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nThis is because the sum \\(x^0 + x^1 + \\dots + x^{2016}\\) is a geometric series with the sum formula for a geometric series:\n\n\\[S = \\frac{x - x^{2017}}{1 - x} = \\frac{x - (2x - 1)}{1 - x} = \\frac{1 - x}{1 - x} = 1.\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nFrom the given equation \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\), we substitute \\(x^{2017}\\) in the numerator:\n\n\\[\\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{2}.\\]",
